This time you've hit a real bug that has prevented fitting mark-resight models when there is zero 'usage' at any detector, since October (secr 4.4.7). That's when I started using the C++ Boost external libraries for all statistical distributions. 'zero expected, zero count' is a domain error for the Poisson distribution iIn Boost, and this needed to be intercepted. I've fixed it in the pre-release version 4.5.4 available as Windows binary secr_4.5.4.zip <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/zip/secr_4.5.4.zip> and source code secr_4.5.4.tar.gz <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/zip/secr_4.5.4.tar.gz>.

Let us know if this doesn't do work for you. Thanks for narrowing down the problem and reporting it.
Murray

