It's a little hard to tell as you switch case and do not give all the models, but I expect this is due to the default behaviour of secr >=4.0 to collapse multiple occasions at proximity detectors within a session, whenever this is 'safe'. This is fast when it works, but unfortunately it can lead to inconsistencies such as you have found. You can take control by setting details = list(fastproximity = FALSE) for all models. See secr-version4.pdf <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-version4.pdf>.
Murray

